.TH EVENTS 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Events \- synthetic keyboard and mouse input injection
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Events
module simulates OS-level keyboard and mouse events.
On POSIX requires X11 with the XTest extension.
On Windows uses the Win32 SendInput / SetCursorPos APIs.
.PP
Key codes on POSIX are X11 keysyms; on Windows they are VK_* virtual key codes.
Mouse button codes: 0=left, 1=right, 2=middle.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS key_down
none() key_down(key: int())
.br
Press (but do not release) a keyboard key.
.SS key_up
none() key_up(key: int())
.br
Release a keyboard key.
.SS key_press
none() key_press(key: int())
.br
Press and immediately release a keyboard key.
.SS mouse_move
none() mouse_move(x: int(), y: int())
.br
Move the mouse cursor to screen coordinates (x, y).
.SS mouse_down
none() mouse_down(button: int())
.br
Press (but do not release) a mouse button (0=left, 1=right, 2=middle).
.SS mouse_up
none() mouse_up(button: int())
.br
Release a mouse button.
.SS mouse_click
none() mouse_click(button: int())
.br
Press and immediately release a mouse button.
.SS mouse_click_every
none() mouse_click_every(button: int(), interval: int(), escape_key: int())
.br
Repeatedly clicks
.I button
every
.I interval
milliseconds until
.I escape_key
is held down.
This call
.B blocks
until the escape key is detected.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
System(3)
